  "tagline": "Columnar storage engine for fast analytics on fast-changing data, paired with Impala or Spark.",
  "description": "Apache Kudu is a distributed columnar storage engine from the Hadoop ecosystem that fills the gap between HDFS/Parquet (fast scans, no updates) and HBase (fast updates, slow scans). Tables have primary keys and support inserts, updates and deletes with low latency, replicated with Raft, while keeping columnar scan performance. It has no SQL of its own; Impala, Spark or Presto/Trino provide the query layer. Kudu remains useful in Cloudera estates for mutable analytic tables, but releases are infrequent and Iceberg or Paimon now cover many of the same needs.",
